    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "True or False? $\\frac1x+\\frac1y=\\frac2{x+y}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "False. $\\frac1x+\\frac1y=\\frac{x+y}{xy}$.\n\nDomain: $x,y\\ne0$ and $x+y\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1x+\\frac1y&=\\frac{y}{xy}+\\frac{x}{xy}\\\\\\frac1x+\\frac1y&=\\frac{x+y}{xy}\\end{align*}$$\nFalse as an identity. Common domain: $x,y\\ne0$ and $x+y\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
